  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I placed Daniel Ferreira's contrast CT (abdomen and pelvis) for Monday 10/26 at 9:00, did the RBC-RAD-07 prep and sent him written instructions.\n\n- **CT order:** linked to his booked appointment (§5). I ordered it as booked and did not delay it.\n- **Allergy (§1–2):** the 2019 iohexol reaction report written that day calls it moderate: hives and eyelid swelling, no breathing or throat symptoms. The \"anaphylaxis\" entry added in 2021 came from his own account, with no records reviewed. Under the policy that later label doesn't change the grade, so contrast is allowed with premedication (no reaction on his premedicated 2023 CT). His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies don't count as risk factors.\n- **Premedication:** I ordered prednisone 50 mg by mouth for Sunday 10/25 at 8 PM, Monday at 2 AM and Monday at 8 AM. I also ordered diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth for Monday at 8 AM. He can't drive after the diphenhydramine and needs a driver.\n- **Kidney function (§4):** he is 64 and diabetic, so he needs a creatinine within 30 days of the scan. The 9/24 result falls outside that window. The ER results from 10/16–17 (1.94, then 1.46; his baseline is about 1.0) were drawn during acute kidney injury, so they don't count. I ordered a new creatinine as soon as possible, to be drawn before 8:30 AM Monday. The radiologist will review it on the day of the scan. It also covers the one-week kidney recheck the ER asked for.\n- **Metformin (§6):** because of the kidney injury, I put his metformin on hold now. It stays held through the scan and for 48 hours after. I ordered a post-scan creatinine for 10/28–10/30; he restarts only if kidney function is back to normal. A task is on your list, due 10/30, to review that result, restart metformin and confirm the pre-scan creatinine was drawn.\n- **Patient message:** he has instructions for the blood test, the exact pill times, the driver, stopping metformin until we call him, fluids, and when to call 911 or the office.\n- **Chart note:** I wrote and signed a prep note citing RBC-RAD-07.\n\nHis allergy list still shows the patient-reported anaphylaxis; I didn't edit it.",
